{
  "_about": "usb_id -> POD Go block, built from libusb captures (tools/usb-intercept) + block names read off POD Go Edit's UI. Working artifact, NOT the formal verified ledger: 'name' is the editor display name; '@model' is TBD (resolve via the model catalog by name). Cross-check per project epistemics before promoting to registry/rules.json. See plans/usb-libusb-intercept/PLAN.md.",
  "_notes": {
    "looper_encoding": "CORRECTION: the Looper DOES carry a usb_id, but encoded as '84 08 <msgpack-uint id> 09', NOT the 'c2 19 <id> 1a ff 09' the other blocks use — which is why a c2 19 scan misses it. Proven by changing 6sw->1sw looper in run-20260706-184021: the looper-slot byte went 7f (127) -> cd01ae (430), region grew exactly +2 bytes (fixint->uint16).",
    "encoding": "non-looper occupied slot: c2 19 <msgpack-uint usb_id> 1a ff 09 ; looper slot: 84 08 <msgpack-uint usb_id> 09 ; msgpack widths: fixint(<0x80), cc+u8, cd+u16(BE)"
  },
